Overall Pipeline (What you should build)
WESAD raw signals → HR extraction → HRV features → ML model → saved .pkl → main.py inference
📁 Suggested Project Structure
project/
│── train_HR.py        # training pipeline
│── main.py            # inference / real-time or test prediction
│── hrv_features.py    # feature extraction logic
│── model.pkl          # saved model
│── scaler.pkl         # feature scaler
│── data/


Step 1: HRV Feature Extraction

You need these core features:

RMSSD → short-term variability (stress-sensitive)
SDNN → overall variability
LF/HF ratio → autonomic balance

👉 Use libraries:

numpy
scipy
neurokit2 (highly recommended)
Example (hrv_features.py)

Step 2: Training Script (train_HR.py)
Key Steps:
Load WESAD data
Extract HRV features per segment
Encode labels
Train model
Save model
Example Training Code

