🎯 How to Reach ≥85% Accuracy

This is the critical part 👇

1. Use Proper Segmentation
Split ECG into 30–60 sec windows
Extract features per window
2. Balance Classes
WESAD is imbalanced → use:
class_weight="balanced"
3. Try Binary First
Stress vs Non-Stress → easier to hit 85%
4. Use More Features (IMPORTANT)

Add:

Mean HR
pNN50
HRV_SDANN
HRV_MeanNN

👉 This alone can boost accuracy a lot

⚠️ Common Mistakes (Avoid These)

❌ Using raw ECG directly in ML
❌ Not segmenting signals
❌ Too few samples (you need MANY windows per subject)
❌ Ignoring normalization

💡 Pro Tip (Very Important)

Your idea from facial recognition is good, but here:

👉 Feature engineering matters more than model choice

Random Forest + good HRV features > Deep learning on raw ECG (for this task)

👍 Final Checklist

✔ HRV features extracted
✔ Model trained (RF/SVM)
✔ Accuracy ≥ 85% (binary easier)
✔ Feature importance plotted
✔ model.pkl + scaler.pkl saved
✔ main.py working
